  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 17272073cbcc03d4b82d101449fb470b, type: 3}
  m_Name: OldTriangle_FirstMeeting
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ProjectCircle.Systems.Dialogue
  speaker: Old Triangle
  lines:
  - ...A circle? Out here, alone?
  - Forgive me. My eyes are not what they were. Neither is the rest of me.
  - I had three vertices once, like any proper Triangle. Then one broke... and my
    own kind cast me out.
  - Do you hear it? That whisper under everything? The Shapeshifter.
  - It takes hold of us through our corners. The more vertices a shape has, the tighter
    its grip.
  - But you... you have none. It cannot find a single corner on you.
  - ...Perhaps that is why you are still yourself. Perhaps that is what it fears.
  - Go on, little circle. Before it notices I am still awake.
